    "result": "Excellent! The frai-core test suite now passes completely. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **`packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`**\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export but it was only available in the default export\n   - Maintained the default export for backward compatibility\n\n### 2. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`**\n   - Updated `toxicityMetric` function signature from `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`\n   - The function was being called with `(outputs, references)` by `runEvaluations`, but was treating the references array as banned terms, causing false positives\n   - Now it accepts references as the second parameter and uses default banned terms correctly\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests in frai-core pass\n\u2705 All 11 tests in frai-gate pass  \n\u2705 No regressions in the full test suite\n\u2705 All public exports remain functional",
